      "content": "That really captures the paternalistic tone well. To round out the speech for the debate, I think it needs to address the \"moral\" dimension that was so prominent back then. Could you have the official describe the specific character or temperament differences they would observe? For example, how would they describe the nature of these local populations compared to Europeans, particularly regarding their ability to handle responsibility, self-discipline, or intellectual pursuits? It would help the students see exactly how the colonialists used these perceived \"inherent traits\" to justify their control.",
